  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Back in the kitchen, Leva tries to assert his new authority as the temporary head chef. He orders the cooks to work faster. Senya and Fedya support him and joke about switching to Terminator mode. Let us listen to their conversation in Russian first.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ребята, давайте работать быстрее.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "У нас ещё три блюда.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Сейчас мы всё сделаем.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Ну, чего вы стоите?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Шеф сказал работать быстрее.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Молодец, Лёва.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Ты хороший шеф.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да, молодец.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Ну что, мы включаем режим терминатора?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да, включаем.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Тогда быстрее за работу.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Терминатор готов готовить еду.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Отлично, давайте быстрее.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Всё будет готово вовремя.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let us examine the conversation line by line.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ребята, давайте работать быстрее.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Guys, let's work faster.' Lyova links 'the boys' directly with 'let's' to express the thought clearly.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "У нас ещё три блюда.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'We still have three dishes.' Russian leaves out 'am', 'is', or 'are' in the present tense, linking 'us' straight to 'of dish'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Сейчас мы всё сделаем.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'We will do everything now.' Here 'now' sets up the idea, while 'we'll do' comes at the end for emphasis.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Ну, чего вы стоите?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Well, why are you standing?' Notice how 'oh' sets up the clause and leads naturally into 'are standing'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Шеф сказал работать быстрее.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'The chef said to work faster.' — Notice the proper name meaning 'chef, boss' paired with the verb for 'said'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Молодец, Лёва.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Well done, Leva.' Notice how 'well done' sets up the clause and leads naturally into 'Lyova'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Ты хороший шеф.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You are a good chef.' Senya uses the informal singular 'you' here with 'chef', as friends and close colleagues do. Then Lyova responds.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да, молодец.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yes, well done.' Lyova links 'yes' directly with 'well done' to express the thought clearly.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Ну что, мы включаем режим терминатора?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Well, are we switching on Terminator mode?' Russian forms this yes-or-no question without a question word, relying on rising pitch on 'Terminator'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да, включаем.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yes, we are switching it on.' Lyova starts with 'we're switching on' and pairs it with 'we're switching on' to make the point clear. Senya answers straight away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Тогда быстрее за работу.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Then faster to work.' Senya links 'back then' directly with 'faster' to express the thought clearly. Then Fedya responds.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Терминатор готов готовить еду.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'The terminator is ready to cook food.' Fedya links 'Terminator' directly with 'ready' to express the thought clearly.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Отлично, давайте быстрее.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Excellent, let's go faster.' This everyday Russian sentence pairs 'perfect' with 'faster'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Всё будет готово вовремя.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Everything will be ready on time.' Notice how 'everything' sets up the clause and leads naturally into 'at the right time'. Now let us listen to the conversation once again.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
